          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "By staying informed, seeking support and guidance when needed, and making healthy decisions, you can build a strong foundation for your life ahead."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.152,
            0.309,
            0.173
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In a Nutshell"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.197,
            0.743,
            0.254
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Adolescence is the period of change from childhood to adulthood. It generally begins around the age of 10 years and usually lasts until 19 years."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.78,
            0.149,
            0.9,
            0.252
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 4,
              "bbox": [
                0.78,
                0.149,
                0.9,
                0.252
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_12_image_4.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.256,
            0.743,
            0.295
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Adolescence is marked by significant and characteristic physical, biological, and emotional changes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.297,
            0.743,
            0.353
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Features that help to distinguish the male from the female but are not directly involved in reproduction are called secondary sexual characteristics."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.356,
            0.744,
            0.412
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Puberty is the stage in which the body of a child undergoes observable and internal changes to develop into an adult capable of reproduction."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.414,
            0.744,
            0.508
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Adolescence in girls is also marked by start of the menstrual cycle, during which there is a discharge of blood generally after every 28–30 days, a process called menstruation. Menstruation begins at puberty and generally ends by the age of 45–55 years."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.511,
            0.719,
            0.531
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Adolescents face several emotional and behavioural changes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.533,
            0.743,
            0.59
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Eating a balanced and healthy diet, maintaining good personal hygiene, and participating in physical activities help adolescents to stay healthy."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.592,
            0.743,
            0.649
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Addictive substances, such as tobacco, alcohol, and drugs, have adverse effects on the body and mind. It is wise to say ‘NO’ to these substances and stay away from them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.651,
            0.743,
            0.707
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Changes that take place in the body during adolescence are primarily controlled by certain chemicals produced in the body. These chemicals are called hormones."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.71,
            0.743,
            0.75
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Proper guidance and awareness help adolescents manage physical, emotional, and behavioural changes effectively."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.761,
            0.515,
            0.783
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let Us Enhance Our Learning"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.807,
            0.743,
            0.864
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Ramesh, an 11-year-old boy, developed a few pimples on his face. His mother told him that this is because of ongoing biological changes in his body."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.161,
            0.867,
            0.743,
            0.906
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) What could be the possible reasons for the development of these pimples on his face?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.156,
            0.91,
            0.727,
            0.931
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) What can he do to get some relief from these pimples?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "aside_text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.958,
            0.119,
            0.981,
            0.413
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Adolescence: A Stage of Growth and Change"
            }
          ]
        },
